Z||000000||WGraffiKs||09-23-1999||04:04 PM||||My wipers give a single sweep (mist) from time-to-time all by themselves.  Sometimes it also happens when I use the signals.  I suspect the wiring insulation in the column has rubbed through, and the wire is shorting intermittantly.  I've seen this in other Fiero's also.  Is it the wiring, or something else?  I could replace the stalk, but with the cruise control on it too, I suspect it will cost big bucks, if it's even available. Is there a connector in the column that connects the stalk wiring to a harness?<BR> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||BOILERMAKER||09-23-1999||04:39 PM||||I had somewhat of the same problem and it ended up being my windshield wiper module.||||reg||1
Z||000002||WGraffiKs||09-24-1999||01:10 AM||||Where is this module located?  My Haynes manual doesn't seem to mention it.  The earlier post (8/6/99) was supposed to cover this topic, but it's GONE!||||reg||2
Z||000003||DJRice||09-24-1999||09:11 AM||||The module is the whole wiper motor deal and its associated electronics under the hood.  I believe the problem was some bad contacts, but youd have to find the old post.||||reg||1
Z||000004||BOILERMAKER||09-24-1999||09:54 AM||||In the manual it had some electrical diagnostics for the wiper system.  When I went through these diagnostics, one of the wires didn't become hot (battery voltage) when it was supposed to.  I would imagine that all I have to do is tear the old module/wiper motor apart and fix it, but I haven't had the time to do so.<P>I replaced the motor and it was like new.||||reg||1
